    "sp_reviews": {
      "type": "sensol-reviews",
      "settings": {
        "show_section": true,
        "label": "Verified Owners",
        "title": "Endorsed by instructors and advanced practitioners."
      },
      "blocks": {
        "review_1": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "I have been teaching Pilates for 12 years and I am very particular about equipment. The RS02 PRO's enhanced cable system is the closest thing to studio-grade I have felt in a home reformer. The smoothness through the full range is remarkable — no catching, no jerky transitions. I use it for my own practice and for private clients at home. The digital weight is a revelation for client sessions — I can set exactly 8.5 kg for a shoulder exercise and know it is precise. This has replaced my studio reformer for everything except group classes.",
            "name": "Mikaela S.",
            "role": "Certified Pilates Instructor, Adelaide"
          }
        },
        "review_2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "After 8 years of reformer Pilates, I was ready for something more. The PRO's enhanced cables opened movement pathways I could only access in the studio. The 145° arms mean I can do overhead work and low-angle rows that no other home reformer offers. The Off-centre mode with the enhanced cables is incredible for rotational patterns. I was hesitant about the $400 premium over the standard RS02, but the cable feel alone justifies it. If you are serious about your practice, this is the one.",
            "name": "Tom H.",
            "role": "Brisbane"
          }
        },
        "review_3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "As a triathlete, I need my cross-training to be targeted and efficient. The PRO's 145° arms let me hit the exact muscle groups my coach prescribed — gluteus medius, rotator cuff, posterior chain. The enhanced cable system's diagonal and rotational patterns mirror the functional demands of my sport better than any spring reformer ever did. I do 30-minute sessions three times a week and my imbalances have noticeably improved. The app tracks everything and the AI coach adjusts my programme based on my training load. Outstanding.",
            "name": "Lisa M.",
            "role": "Competitive Triathlete, Gold Coast"
          }
        },
        "review_4": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "text": "I have trained on Balanced Body and Merrithew studio reformers for years. The PRO is not identical — nothing at this price point would be — but it is remarkably close. The enhanced cables give a smooth, consistent feel that I did not expect from a digital weight system. The 0.5 kg precision is actually better than springs for controlled progression. Lost one star because I would like to see more instructor-led advanced classes in the app, though they are adding content regularly. For home use, this is exceptional value.",
            "name": "Daniel R.",
            "role": "Sydney"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "review_1",
        "review_2",
        "review_3",
        "review_4"
      ]
    },
    "sp_qa": {
      "type": "sensol-product-qa",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Questions & Answers",
        "title": "Common questions.",
        "open_first": true
      },
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between the RS02 and the RS02 PRO?",
            "answer": "The RS02 PRO adds two key upgrades over the standard RS02: an enhanced Pilates cable system that provides smoother tension, expanded movement pathways, and more advanced sequencing capability; and 0–145° arm articulation (vs 0–132° on the standard RS02), opening additional exercise angles. Both models share the same digital weight system, motor, app, training modes, and footprint. The PRO is designed for serious practitioners who need the enhanced cable feel and wider arm range."
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the RS02 PRO worth the extra $400 over the RS02?",
            "answer": "If you are an experienced Pilates practitioner, an instructor, or someone who values the quality of movement feel, absolutely. The enhanced cable system provides a noticeably smoother, more professional experience that serious practitioners will appreciate every session. The 145° arm range opens exercise angles that the standard RS02 cannot reach. For casual users or beginners, the standard RS02 may be sufficient. For those who can feel the difference, the PRO is worth every dollar."
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can the RS02 PRO replace my studio membership?",
            "answer": "For most advanced practitioners, yes. The PRO's enhanced cable system delivers a studio-level feel, the 300+ app classes include advanced sequences, and the AI coaching provides personalised progression. The 200+ movements cover virtually everything you would do in a studio session. The main thing you lose is the social aspect of group classes and hands-on instructor adjustments — but you gain convenience, privacy, and significant cost savings."
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the enhanced cable system work?",
            "answer": "The enhanced cable system uses upgraded pulleys and cable guides that reduce friction and provide smoother tension throughout the full range of motion. Additional cable anchor points create new angles of pull, expanding the available movement pathways beyond what standard cables or springs can offer. The result is a feel that mirrors professional studio equipment — consistent, fluid, and responsive."
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the RS02 PRO suitable for Pilates instructors?",
            "answer": "Yes. Many features make the PRO ideal for instructors: the studio-level cable feel satisfies professional standards, the digital weight system allows precise resistance prescription for clients, the 145° arms enable a full range of assisted exercises, and the app tracks client progress. Instructors can use the PRO for their own practice, for private client sessions at home, or as a demonstration tool. The enhanced cable system meets the quality expectations that professional instructors demand."
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What exercises can I do on the PRO that I cannot do on the standard RS02?",
            "answer": "The 145° arm range (vs 132° on the RS02) enables full overhead press positions, low-angle decline work, and extended-range rows. The enhanced cable system's additional anchor points enable diagonal pull patterns, rotational movements, and advanced unilateral sequences that require specific cable pathways. These movements are particularly valuable for athletic cross-training, advanced Pilates sequences, and functional movement training."
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a subscription for the app?",
            "answer": "No. The Vesta Sensol App is included free with your RS02 PRO purchase. You get full access to 300+ guided classes (including PRO-specific advanced sequences), AI-driven coaching, workout analytics, and all app features with no monthly fees. This is a significant advantage over competitors like NordicTrack ($60/month) and Frame Fitness ($39.99/month)."
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty and return policy?",
            "answer": "The RS02 PRO comes with a Lifetime Warranty covering manufacturing defects, including the enhanced cable system. We also offer a 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee — if you are not satisfied within 30 days of delivery, return it for a full refund. Free domestic shipping is included for all Australian orders."
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the RS02 PRO compare to studio reformers like Balanced Body?",
            "answer": "The Balanced Body Allegro 2 (~$6,000+ AUD) is the studio standard, known for its smooth carriage and quality construction. The RS02 PRO matches that smoothness with its enhanced cable system while adding features no studio reformer offers: digital weight with 0.5 kg precision, dual-function design (reformer + strength), AI coaching, three training modes, and app connectivity. The PRO costs less than half the price of a Balanced Body while offering significantly more versatility."
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does delivery take and is shipping really free?",
            "answer": "Yes, shipping is completely free to all Australian addresses. Orders are dispatched within 2–3 business days. Standard delivery takes 5–10 business days depending on your location. You will receive tracking information once your order has been dispatched. The RS02 PRO ships in a single package weighing approximately 63 kg."
          }
        }
      },
